  "body": "## What\n\n- Add `scripts/reviewer-gh.sh` and a shell module that resolve the `tbhbbot` token for each command, verify the effective account, and fail closed before a review command can run.\n- Add pure review policy functions with table, property, and process fixtures.\n- Update AGENTS.md, the workflow page, plan, and briefs for review rounds, current approval, five required checks, branch updates, and operator merge boundaries.\n\n## Why\n\nThe default implementer account is `tbhb`. Reviews need a separate recorded identity, and workers need the live approval and branch rules before they publish or update a PR.\n\n## Evidence\n\nHarness: Codex CLI 0.157.1. Model: `gpt-6-sol` at medium effort.\n\n[Reviewer account evidence](https://github.com/tbhb/agent-orchestration-poc/blob/process/83-review-process/reports/inputs/reviewer-account-evidence.md) records the REST ruleset reads, safe identity probes, fixture outcomes, source commit, sandbox limits, and exact check commands. Local `mise run check` and `mise run check:mutation` passed. The integration fixtures passed with `--run-integration`.\n\nSize: 301 changed Python and shell code lines, counting test modules and excluding JSON fixtures, prose, and evidence. This is below the 400-line target.\n\nThe issue's allowed paths omit `mise.toml`, so `mise run check:review-identity` remains unavailable even though the direct fixture commands pass. The issue review comment requested a path adjustment before dispatch. The blocked-merge and update-approval observations are operator recorded without a new raw trace in this worktree.\n\n## Docs\n\nUpdated AGENTS.md, the workflow page, project plan, both documentation briefs, and the evidence report. The local docs link check could not launch Chromium under the macOS sandbox and reported three pre-existing `/workflow/` link failures. The hosted docs check passed.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] CI green\n- [x] Docs updated\n- [x] No secrets in staged changes or evidence\n- [x] Evidence committed\n\nRefs: #83\n",
